## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design modular, scalable NLP systems that evolve without full retraining, while meeting strict latency and privacy constraints across multiple languages.

## Key Concepts
- Adapter-based fine-tuning
- Multilingual encoders
- Real-time latency requirements
- Privacy-preserving logging
- Canary rollout and drift detection

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example of adding an adapter for a new intent using adapters
const tokenizer = loadTokenizer("xlm-roberta-base");
const model = loadModelWithHeads("xlm-roberta-base");
model.addAdapter("refund_policy_update");
model.trainAdapter("refund_policy_update");
// fine-tune with a few hundred examples
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate that new intents do not degrade existing ones?
- How would you handle multilingual data drift across EN/ES/PT?

## Why This Is Asked
Addresses real-time multilingual safety, reduces model hallucinations, and tight latency with on-device processing and privacy-preserving checks.

## Key Concepts
- Retrieval-Augmented Generation
- On-device inference
- External verifier for factuality
- Drift detection and explainability
- Auditable rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-pipeline wiring
const stream = createLiveStream(source);
stream.map(msg => translateToEN(msg)).then(en => {
  const intent = classifyIntent(en);
  const knowledge = fetchKB(en, intent);
  const reply = generatePolicyResponse(knowledge, en);
  if (verifyWithSources(reply, knowledge)) emit(reply);
});
```

